.\" Version: 1.2
.\"
.TH SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout 8 "06 Oct 2026" "" "SAPHanaSR"
.\"
.SH NAME
.\"
SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout \- Alert agent for cluster resources timeout alerts.
.PP
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\"
SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout can be used to react on Linux cluster resources timeout
alerts.
.PP
The Linux cluster provides an interface to initiate external actions when a
cluster event occurs (alert). Than the cluster calls an external program (an
alert agent) to handle that alert.
.PP
When a Linux cluster resource agent runs into resources timeout, the cluster can
call SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout on each active cluster node. Main purpose is colleting
data in case of resource agent timeouts.
.br
See also manual pages SAPHanaSR-hookHelper(8) and ocf_suse_SAPHanaController(7).
.PP
.B SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout is a technology preview.
.PP
.\"
.SH SUPPORTED PARAMETERS
.TP
\fBtimeout\fR
If the alert agent does not complete within this amount of time, it will be terminated.
Optional, default "30s", minimum "30s", example "meta timeout=30s".
.TP
\fBalert_sid\fR
SAP SID of the instance to handle. Might be used by custom helper scripts.
Optional, default "HA1", example "attributes alert_sid=ADA".
.TP
\fBalert_ino\fR
SAP instance number of instance to handle. Might be used by custom helper scripts.
Optional, default "00", example "attributes alert_ino=22".
.TP
\fBalert_cmd\fR
Command to call. Might be used to name a custom helper script.
SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout calls the command like
.br
(sudo "$alert_cmd" "$alert_subcmd" "$alert_sid" "$alert_ino" 2>&1).
.br
Optional, default "/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-helper", example "alert_cmd=/usr/local/bin/dumpstack".
.TP
\fBalert_subcmd\fR
Subcommand to call SAPHanaSR-hookHelper or custom script with.
Optional, default "alertLog".
.br
See manual page SAPHanaSR-hookHelper(8).
.PP
.\"
.SH RETURN CODES
.\"
.B 0
Successful program execution.
.br
.B >0
Usage, syntax or execution errors.
.br
In addition log entries are written, which can be scanned by using a pattern
like "SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout".
.PP
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.\"
\fB*\fR Simple example configuration for the resources timeout alert agent.
.PP
The following lines needs to be added to the cluster´s CIB:
.PP
.RS 2
alert resources-1 "/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout" \\
.br
 select resources
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Simple example for configuring the alert agent by using crm.
.PP
Alternate way for configuring the alert agent.
.PP
.RS 2
# crm configure alert resources-1 \\
.br
 "/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout" \\
.br
 select resources
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Advanced example configuration for the resources timeout alert agent.
.PP
A custom script /usr/local/bin/dumpstack is used, SID is ADA, instance number 00.
The resulting call is:
.br
 /usr/local/bin/dumpstack trace ADA 00
.PP
.RS 2
alert resources-1 "/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout" \\
.br
 select resources \\
.br
 attributes alert_sid=ADA alert_ino=00 \\
.br 
 alert_cmd="/usr/local/bin/dumpstack" alert_subcmd="trace"
.RE
.PP
.PP
\fB*\fR Showing alert agent messages.
.PP
.RS 2
# grep SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout /var/log/messages
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Showing alert agent helper messages.
.PP
.RS 2
# grep SAPHanaSR-hookHelper.*alertLog /var/log/messages
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Example for sudo permissions in /etc/sudoers.d/SAPHanaSR .
.PP
See also manual pages sudoers(5) and SAPHanaSR-hookHelper(8).
.PP
.RS 2
# SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout needs
.br
hacluster ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-hookHelper --sid=HA1 --case=alertLog
.RE
.PP
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout
the alert agent
.TP
/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-hookHelper
the default alert agent helper
.TP
/etc/sudoers.d/
directory for sudoers config files
.PP
.\"
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.\"
* SAPHanaSR-alert-timeout should be activated only, when requested by support.
.PP
* No other alert agent should be configured for the resources alert.
.PP
* User hacluster is member of group haclient. Both are defined locally on all
cluster nodes.
.PP
* User hacluster needs password-less sudo permission on "/usr/bin/SAPHanaSR-hookHelper".
If a custom script is used, respective permissions might be needed.
.PP
* The customer is responsible for any custom script called by the alert agent.
Any custom script should return within the alert agent timeout.
.PP
.\" TODO * To allow SAPHanaSR-hookHelper command "stack", gdb is needed.
.\" .PP
* To allow SAPHanaSR-hookHelper command "alertLog", ClusterTool2 3.1.4 or newer is needed.
.PP
* The alert agent runtime almost completely depends on call-outs to OS and
Linux cluster. The alert agent timeout should be 30s at least.
.PP
